    "name": "Greek Tag",
    "description": "<p data-start=\"198\" data-end=\"533\">Greek Tag is a campus-wide interactive fundraising game where participants are assigned a randomly selected &ldquo;target&rdquo; and must locate and spray them with Silly String. Once a player successfully sprays their assigned target, they receive a new target and continue in the game. The objective is to be the last participant remaining.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"535\" data-end=\"914\">The game will take place over the course of several days across campus and is designed to encourage engagement, friendly competition, and participation from members of the Drexel community. Participants will pay a small entry fee to join the game, with all proceeds supporting <strong data-start=\"812\" data-end=\"838\">The Ability Experience</strong>, Pi Kappa Phi&rsquo;s national philanthropy that serves people with disabilities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"1257\">All gameplay will follow campus safety guidelines. Tagging will only occur in approved public areas on campus (designated zones), and restricted locations such as classrooms, academic buildings during class, workplaces, and private residences will be off-limits. The game is intended to promote community involvement while raising funds for a meaningful cause.</p>",
